{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-119267","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-196227","text":"Weave — a static cost certificate for the [&] stack's resource rung"}]},{"id":"blk-119268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196228","text":"A research prototype, built invariant-first: find the invariants, state the rules, enforce them in code, close the loop. Plain Node (v18+), no dependencies. Run any script with "},{"id":"spn-196229","marks":["code"],"text":"node <path>"},{"id":"spn-196230","text":" (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-196231","marks":["code"],"text":"node src/weave.mjs"},{"id":"spn-196232","text":"), or use the npm scripts: "},{"id":"spn-196233","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run demo"},{"id":"spn-196234","text":", "},{"id":"spn-196235","marks":["code"],"text":"npm test"},{"id":"spn-196236","text":", "},{"id":"spn-196237","marks":["code"],"text":"npm run proofs"},{"id":"spn-196238","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-119269","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196239","marks":["bold"],"text":"Positioning (read `weave-and-the-ampersand-stack.md` first)."},{"id":"spn-196240","text":" Weave began as \"a better Bend/HVM,\" but with box-and-box and OpenSentience in frame that framing is wrong. Weave is "},{"id":"spn-196241","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-196242","text":" a Bend/HVM competitor — it is a deep probe of one rung of the [&] stack: the "},{"id":"spn-196243","marks":["bold"],"text":"resource rung"},{"id":"spn-196244","text":" (the affine ledger, \"can we afford it\"), and specifically the piece box-and-box doesn't yet have — a "},{"id":"spn-196245","marks":["bold"],"text":"static cost certificate"},{"id":"spn-196246","text":" computed before a computation runs, not a runtime meter read after. HVM4 (now on GitHub in early preview) is the intended execution backend; the cost certificate is substrate-independent, so lowering to HVM4 is an execution choice, not a correctness dependency."}]},{"id":"blk-119270","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-196247","text":"New here? Check the proof, don't take my word for it"}]},{"id":"blk-119271","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196248","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"./proofs/"}],"text":"`proofs/`"},{"id":"spn-196249","text":" holds "},{"id":"spn-196250","marks":["bold"],"text":"proof you can verify without running anything"},{"id":"spn-196251","text":" from committed text — no install, no run. Read "},{"id":"spn-196252","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"./proofs/README.md"}],"text":"`proofs/README.md`"},{"id":"spn-196253","text":", then eyeball "},{"id":"spn-196254","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"./proofs/RECEIPTS.txt"}],"text":"`proofs/RECEIPTS.txt`"},{"id":"spn-196255","text":" (the static cost grade vs. measured growth, checkable by finite differences; the falsifiable soundness predicate; a cross-check against the independent HVM4 runtime) and "},{"id":"spn-196256","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"./proofs/transcripts/"}],"text":"`proofs/transcripts/`"},{"id":"spn-196257","text":" (the exact stdout of every script, claim-by-claim). Regenerate with "},{"id":"spn-196258","marks":["code"],"text":"node proofs/generate.mjs"},{"id":"spn-196259","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-196260","marks":["code"],"text":"node tools/regenerate-proofs.mjs"},{"id":"spn-196261","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-119272","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-196262","text":"Layout"}]},{"id":"blk-119273","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"weave/\n  README.md                            this file\n  proofs/     RECEIPTS.txt (by-hand-checkable) + transcripts/ (per-script) + generate.mjs + README.md\n  src/        the engine (pure library, exports an API; each runs a demo when invoked directly)\n  test/       the validation suites (differential / property / soundness / cross-engine)\n  surface/    weave_surface.exs        the Elixir macro front-end\n  tools/      regenerate-proofs.mjs    rebuilds proofs/transcripts/ (--check verifies no drift)\n  docs/        positioning + design docs"},{"id":"blk-119274","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-196263","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/"},{"id":"spn-196264","text":" — read these first"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-119276","spans":[{"id":"spn-196265","text":"File"}]},{"id":"blk-119277","spans":[{"id":"spn-196266","text":"What it is"}]}],"id":"blk-119275","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-119278","spans":[{"id":"spn-196267","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/weave-and-the-ampersand-stack.md"}]},{"id":"blk-119279","spans":[{"id":"spn-196268","marks":["bold"],"text":"Start here."},{"id":"spn-196269","text":" Repositions Weave inside the [&] stack, grades the stack against the AIOS agent-OS reference (gap analysis), and specifies the cost-certificate → resource-rung integration and the HVM4 backend plan."}]}],[{"id":"blk-119280","spans":[{"id":"spn-196270","marks":["code"],"text":"docs/weave-design.md"}]},{"id":"blk-119281","spans":[{"id":"spn-196271","text":"The design doc: thesis, openings in Bend, the five invariants, the closed loop. "},{"id":"spn-196272","marks":["bold"],"text":"Read after the positioning doc — it predates the [&]-stack reframe and the validation work, so treat it as the starting hypothesis."}]}]]},{"id":"blk-119282","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-196273","marks":["code"],"text":"src/"},{"id":"spn-196274","text":" — the engine"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-119284","spans":[{"id":"spn-196275","text":"File"}]},{"id":"blk-119285","spans":[{"id":"spn-196276","text":"What it is"}]},{"id":"blk-119286","spans":[{"id":"spn-196277","text":"Run"}]}],"id":"blk-119283","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-119287","spans":[{"id":"spn-196278","marks":["code"],"text":"src/weave.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-119288","spans":[{"id":"spn-196279","text":"The core. An Interaction-Calculus reducer (β + sup/dup, metered, with time and space vetoes), the static invariant checker (affine / label-coherence / κ), and a small superposed-search + evolution loop."}]},{"id":"blk-119289","spans":[{"id":"spn-196280","marks":["code"],"text":"node src/weave.mjs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-119290","spans":[{"id":"spn-196281","marks":["code"],"text":"src/weave-classify.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-119291","spans":[{"id":"spn-196282","text":"Cost as a type, statically. Infers types, reports the iteration "},{"id":"spn-196283","marks":["italic"],"text":"rank"},{"id":"spn-196284","text":" (poly / exp / tower) with no execution, and cross-checks against measured cost."}]},{"id":"blk-119292","spans":[{"id":"spn-196285","marks":["code"],"text":"node src/weave-classify.mjs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-119293","spans":[{"id":"spn-196286","marks":["code"],"text":"src/weave-eal.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-119294","spans":[{"id":"spn-196287","marks":["bold"],"text":"The certificate."},{"id":"spn-196288","text":" Type-directed EAL box-decoration: the static box-nesting "},{"id":"spn-196289","marks":["italic"],"text":"depth"},{"id":"spn-196290","text":" (= certified elementary tower height) with a per-binder certificate. Upgrades the rank proxy toward a real bound."}]},{"id":"blk-119295","spans":[{"id":"spn-196291","marks":["code"],"text":"node src/weave-eal.mjs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-119296","spans":[{"id":"spn-196292","marks":["code"],"text":"src/weave-eal-degree.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-119297","spans":[{"id":"spn-196293","text":"Stage B: recovers the polynomial "},{"id":"spn-196294","marks":["italic"],"text":"degree"},{"id":"spn-196295","text":" inside the depth-1 rung by finite differences — the measured ground truth that static LAL (Baillot–Terui) would prove."}]},{"id":"blk-119298","spans":[{"id":"spn-196296","marks":["code"],"text":"node src/weave-eal-degree.mjs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-119299","spans":[{"id":"spn-196297","marks":["code"],"text":"src/weave-cost.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-119300","spans":[{"id":"spn-196298","text":"The cost cliff, measured: addition (linear), multiplication (polynomial), exponentiation towers (detonate). Shows source size ≠ cost."}]},{"id":"blk-119301","spans":[{"id":"spn-196299","marks":["code"],"text":"node src/weave-cost.mjs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-119302","spans":[{"id":"spn-196300","marks":["code"],"text":"src/weave-hvm4.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-119303","spans":[{"id":"spn-196301","text":"Local round-trip lowering to a generic HVM-core syntax + inverse parser (semantics-preserving validation, no external binary)."}]},{"id":"blk-119304","spans":[{"id":"spn-196302","marks":["code"],"text":"node src/weave-hvm4.mjs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-119305","spans":[{"id":"spn-196303","marks":["code"],"text":"src/weave-backend.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-119306","spans":[{"id":"spn-196304","text":"The \"backend\" the surface lowers to (the Nx/EXLA role): reads an IR term as JSON and runs the real engine."}]},{"id":"blk-119307","spans":[{"id":"spn-196305","marks":["code"],"text":"node src/weave-backend.mjs <op> '<ir-json>'"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-119308","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-196306","marks":["code"],"text":"test/"},{"id":"spn-196307","text":" — the validation suites"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-119310","spans":[{"id":"spn-196308","text":"File"}]},{"id":"blk-119311","spans":[{"id":"spn-196309","text":"What it is"}]},{"id":"blk-119312","spans":[{"id":"spn-196310","text":"Run"}]}],"id":"blk-119309","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-119313","spans":[{"id":"spn-196311","marks":["code"],"text":"test/weave-validate.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-119314","spans":[{"id":"spn-196312","text":"Differential testing: linearize a pure λ-term, reduce with Weave, compare the normal form to a reference normal-order evaluator. "},{"id":"spn-196313","marks":["bold"],"text":"12/12."}]},{"id":"blk-119315","spans":[{"id":"spn-196314","marks":["code"],"text":"node test/weave-validate.mjs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-119316","spans":[{"id":"spn-196315","marks":["code"],"text":"test/weave-proptest.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-119317","spans":[{"id":"spn-196316","text":"Checker-gated property testing over thousands of random simply-typed terms. None mis-evaluated."}]},{"id":"blk-119318","spans":[{"id":"spn-196317","marks":["code"],"text":"node test/weave-proptest.mjs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-119319","spans":[{"id":"spn-196318","marks":["code"],"text":"test/weave-soundness.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-119320","spans":[{"id":"spn-196319","text":"Stress-tests the classifier verdict against measured cost over an adversarial battery + ~2000 random terms. Falsifiable predicate: no rank≤1 term detonated."}]},{"id":"blk-119321","spans":[{"id":"spn-196320","marks":["code"],"text":"node test/weave-soundness.mjs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-119322","spans":[{"id":"spn-196321","marks":["code"],"text":"test/weave-fold-test.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-119323","spans":[{"id":"spn-196322","text":"Differential test for the structural-recursion layer: linearized "},{"id":"spn-196323","marks":["code"],"text":"fold"},{"id":"spn-196324","text":" vs JS ground truth over random lists × {add, mul, sub}. "},{"id":"spn-196325","marks":["bold"],"text":"1200/1200."}]},{"id":"blk-119324","spans":[{"id":"spn-196326","marks":["code"],"text":"node test/weave-fold-test.mjs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-119325","spans":[{"id":"spn-196327","marks":["code"],"text":"test/weave-eal-test.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-119326","spans":[{"id":"spn-196328","text":"Validates the EAL "},{"id":"spn-196329","marks":["bold"],"text":"certificate"},{"id":"spn-196330","text":" against "},{"id":"spn-196331","marks":["italic"],"text":"measured"},{"id":"spn-196332","text":" cost (not the proxy): certified-cheap never detonates, "},{"id":"spn-196333","marks":["code"],"text":"eal:true"},{"id":"spn-196334","text":" reduces oracle-free (no residue), depth matches the validated rank."}]},{"id":"blk-119327","spans":[{"id":"spn-196335","marks":["code"],"text":"node test/weave-eal-test.mjs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-119328","spans":[{"id":"spn-196336","marks":["code"],"text":"test/weave-hvm4-run.mjs"}]},{"id":"blk-119329","spans":[{"id":"spn-196337","text":"The real HVM4 backend: lowers to HVM4 surface syntax, shells to the built binary, and differential-tests integer outputs against the toy reducer. "},{"id":"spn-196338","marks":["bold"],"text":"6/6."},{"id":"spn-196339","text":" Needs "},{"id":"spn-196340","marks":["code"],"text":"~/hvm4/src/hvm"},{"id":"spn-196341","text":" (or "},{"id":"spn-196342","marks":["code"],"text":"HVM4_BIN="},{"id":"spn-196343","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-119330","spans":[{"id":"spn-196344","marks":["code"],"text":"node test/weave-hvm4-run.mjs"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-119331","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-196345","marks":["code"],"text":"surface/"},{"id":"spn-196346","text":" — the Elixir front-end"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-119333","spans":[{"id":"spn-196347","text":"File"}]},{"id":"blk-119334","spans":[{"id":"spn-196348","text":"What it is"}]},{"id":"blk-119335","spans":[{"id":"spn-196349","text":"Run"}]}],"id":"blk-119332","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-119336","spans":[{"id":"spn-196350","marks":["code"],"text":"surface/weave_surface.exs"}]},{"id":"blk-119337","spans":[{"id":"spn-196351","text":"An Elixir macro surface. "},{"id":"spn-196352","marks":["code"],"text":"defweave"},{"id":"spn-196353","text":" compiles native "},{"id":"spn-196354","marks":["code"],"text":"fn"},{"id":"spn-196355","text":" syntax — integer literals, "},{"id":"spn-196356","marks":["code"],"text":"+"},{"id":"spn-196357","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-196358","marks":["code"],"text":"*"},{"id":"spn-196359","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-196360","marks":["code"],"text":"-"},{"id":"spn-196361","text":", list literals, "},{"id":"spn-196362","marks":["code"],"text":"fold"},{"id":"spn-196363","text":" — into Weave IR at compile time, then shells to "},{"id":"spn-196364","marks":["code"],"text":"../src/weave-backend.mjs"},{"id":"spn-196365","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-119338","spans":[{"id":"spn-196366","marks":["code"],"text":"elixir surface/weave_surface.exs"}]}],[{"id":"blk-119339","spans":[{"id":"spn-196367","marks":["code"],"text":"surface/weave_govern.exs"}]},{"id":"blk-119340","spans":[{"id":"spn-196368","marks":["bold"],"text":"The stack, end to end."},{"id":"spn-196369","text":" Authors four plans with "},{"id":"spn-196370","marks":["code"],"text":"defweave"},{"id":"spn-196371","text":", certifies each one's cost class with "},{"id":"spn-196372","marks":["code"],"text":"Weave.classify"},{"id":"spn-196373","text":" (static — no execution), shells to the box-and-box governance kernel (the highest-utility exponential is "},{"id":"spn-196374","marks":["bold"],"text":"annihilated"},{"id":"spn-196375","text":" "},{"id":"spn-196376","marks":["code"],"text":"0̲"},{"id":"spn-196377","text":" by the resource-rung floor), "},{"id":"spn-196378","marks":["bold"],"text":"runs"},{"id":"spn-196379","text":" the polynomial winner to a real answer ("},{"id":"spn-196380","marks":["code"],"text":"210"},{"id":"spn-196381","text":"), then runs the refused tower anyway and watches it "},{"id":"spn-196382","marks":["bold"],"text":"detonate"},{"id":"spn-196383","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-196384","marks":["code"],"text":"over-space"},{"id":"spn-196385","text":") — vindicating the static refusal. Cost is a type, and the type decides."}]},{"id":"blk-119341","spans":[{"id":"spn-196386","marks":["code"],"text":"elixir surface/weave_govern.exs"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-119342","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-196387","text":"Honest status"}]},{"id":"blk-119343","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196388","text":"What runs and is validated:"}]},{"id":"blk-119344","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-119346","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196389","text":"The reducer is sound on every term tested — the 12-term battery plus ~3000 random simply-typed"}]}],"id":"blk-119345","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-119347","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196390","text":"terms plus Church arithmetic. No counterexample found."}]},{"id":"blk-119348","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-119350","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196391","text":"The cost cliff is real and measured; the static classifier predicts it from structure before"}]}],"id":"blk-119349","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-119351","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196392","text":"running, and the prediction matches."}]},{"id":"blk-119352","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-119354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196393","marks":["bold"],"text":"Recursion fork: decided."},{"id":"spn-196394","text":" The surface offers "},{"id":"spn-196395","marks":["italic"],"text":"structural"},{"id":"spn-196396","text":" recursion (fold over a list),"}]}],"id":"blk-119353","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-119355","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196397","text":"not a general "},{"id":"spn-196398","marks":["code"],"text":"fix"},{"id":"spn-196399","text":". A Church-encoded list is its own right fold, so recursion on the spine is total, has no fixpoint, and stays in the elementary/certified fragment — the feature is also the limit, by design."}]},{"id":"blk-119356","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-119358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196400","marks":["bold"],"text":"Primitives + a list ADT are in, and the surface is now writable."},{"id":"spn-196401","text":" Native integers and "},{"id":"spn-196402","marks":["code"],"text":"+"},{"id":"spn-196403","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-196404","marks":["code"],"text":"*"},{"id":"spn-196405","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-196406","marks":["code"],"text":"-"}]}],"id":"blk-119357","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-119359","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196407","text":"lower to a strict "},{"id":"spn-196408","marks":["code"],"text":"Op"},{"id":"spn-196409","text":" node (type-order 0, no cost-rank contribution); list literals lower to Church lists; "},{"id":"spn-196410","marks":["code"],"text":"fold"},{"id":"spn-196411","text":" is the list applied. Duplicating an "},{"id":"spn-196412","marks":["code"],"text":"Op"},{"id":"spn-196413","text":"-carrying combiner needed one new rule — "},{"id":"spn-196414","marks":["code"],"text":"OP-SUP"},{"id":"spn-196415","text":", the operator/superposition commutation, exactly parallel to the existing "},{"id":"spn-196416","marks":["code"],"text":"APP-SUP"},{"id":"spn-196417","text":". With it, linearized folds match JS ground truth "},{"id":"spn-196418","marks":["bold"],"text":"1200/1200"},{"id":"spn-196419","text":" over random lists and operators, and "},{"id":"spn-196420","marks":["code"],"text":"sum"},{"id":"spn-196421","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-196422","marks":["code"],"text":"product"},{"id":"spn-196423","text":" over a list literal run end-to-end through Elixir and classify rank-1 polynomial."}]},{"id":"blk-119360","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196424","text":"What is a corrected claim (the validation overturned earlier guesses):"}]},{"id":"blk-119361","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-119363","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196425","text":"An early discussion called Church multiplication the \"oracle boundary.\" That was wrong — it was a"}]}],"id":"blk-119362","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-119364","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196426","text":"missing "},{"id":"spn-196427","marks":["code"],"text":"DUP-APP"},{"id":"spn-196428","text":" commutation rule in the reducer, since fixed. There is no known boundary within the tested fragment."}]},{"id":"blk-119365","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-119367","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196429","text":"The static invariants "},{"id":"spn-196430","marks":["code"],"text":"I1"},{"id":"spn-196431","text":" (affine) + "},{"id":"spn-196432","marks":["code"],"text":"I2"},{"id":"spn-196433","text":" (labels) are "},{"id":"spn-196434","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-196435","text":" sufficient for soundness — a term"}]}],"id":"blk-119366","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-119368","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196436","text":"exists that they accept but a naive reducer mis-evaluates. They are a source-level discipline, not a soundness certificate."}]},{"id":"blk-119369","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196437","text":"What is a heuristic, not a theorem:"}]},{"id":"blk-119370","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-119372","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196438","marks":["code"],"text":"weave-classify"},{"id":"spn-196439","text":" uses STLC type-order as a proxy for the complexity rung. It is principled"}]}],"id":"blk-119371","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-119373","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196440","text":"(higher-order iteration climbs the Grzegorczyk hierarchy) and validated on these families, but it is an under-approximation of full Elementary/Light-Affine inference, reports the ladder "},{"id":"spn-196441","marks":["italic"],"text":"rung"},{"id":"spn-196442","text":" not the polynomial degree, and goes silent on terms that aren't simply-typable."}]},{"id":"blk-119374","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-196443","text":"The thesis, as far as it's earned"}]},{"id":"blk-119375","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196444","text":"The defensible core is substructural: you get a guarantee by removing the structural rule that would let you violate it, so the violation becomes inexpressible. In this style the "},{"id":"spn-196445","marks":["italic"],"text":"safety invariant"},{"id":"spn-196446","text":" and the "},{"id":"spn-196447","marks":["italic"],"text":"cost guarantee"},{"id":"spn-196448","text":" are the same object — linearity-with-stratification simultaneously makes reduction sound, licenses the oracle-free fast path, and grades cost. Two of those faces now have running artifacts (soundness: "},{"id":"spn-196449","marks":["code"],"text":"test/weave-validate"},{"id":"spn-196450","text":"; cost: "},{"id":"spn-196451","marks":["code"],"text":"src/weave-classify"},{"id":"spn-196452","text":"), and all three are exhibited together — checkable by hand — in "},{"id":"spn-196453","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"./proofs/RECEIPTS.txt"}],"text":"`proofs/RECEIPTS.txt`"},{"id":"spn-196454","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-119376","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196455","text":"Placed in the [&] stack, this is the "},{"id":"spn-196456","marks":["bold"],"text":"resource rung"},{"id":"spn-196457","text":" made into a static certificate. box-and-box's resource rung is a "},{"id":"spn-196458","marks":["italic"],"text":"runtime"},{"id":"spn-196459","text":" ledger (\"what was spent\"); Weave is the "},{"id":"spn-196460","marks":["italic"],"text":"static"},{"id":"spn-196461","text":" certificate (\"what can be spent, in what class, with termination guaranteed\"). Wired into "},{"id":"spn-196462","marks":["code"],"text":"govern()"},{"id":"spn-196463","text":", a computation that can't be certified to halt within budget becomes "},{"id":"spn-196464","marks":["code"],"text":"0̄"},{"id":"spn-196465","text":" — annihilated, not down-ranked — the same floor pattern the kernel already uses for forbidden actions. Three of your theses converge here: "},{"id":"spn-196466","marks":["bold"],"text":"symbol-as-system"},{"id":"spn-196467","text":" (the verdict is the arithmetic), "},{"id":"spn-196468","marks":["bold"],"text":"topology-as-warrant"},{"id":"spn-196469","text":" (κ licenses the shape of the reasoning), and "},{"id":"spn-196470","marks":["bold"],"text":"cost-as-certificate"},{"id":"spn-196471","text":" (the discipline that makes the fast path sound is the one that bounds cost). See "},{"id":"spn-196472","marks":["code"],"text":"weave-and-the-ampersand-stack.md"},{"id":"spn-196473","text":" for the full integration and gap analysis."}]},{"id":"blk-119377","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196474","marks":["bold"],"text":"Update — the next step is taken (partway)."},{"id":"spn-196475","text":" "},{"id":"spn-196476","marks":["code"],"text":"src/weave-eal.mjs"},{"id":"spn-196477","text":" now computes a real EAL box-decoration: a static box-nesting "},{"id":"spn-196478","marks":["italic"],"text":"depth"},{"id":"spn-196479","text":" (= certified elementary tower height) with a per-binder certificate, validated against "},{"id":"spn-196480","marks":["italic"],"text":"measured"},{"id":"spn-196481","text":" cost in "},{"id":"spn-196482","marks":["code"],"text":"test/weave-eal-test.mjs"},{"id":"spn-196483","text":" (certified-cheap never detonated; every "},{"id":"spn-196484","marks":["code"],"text":"eal:true"},{"id":"spn-196485","text":" term reduced oracle-free). The depth-1 rung's polynomial "},{"id":"spn-196486","marks":["italic"],"text":"degree"},{"id":"spn-196487","text":" is recovered empirically in "},{"id":"spn-196488","marks":["code"],"text":"src/weave-eal-degree.mjs"},{"id":"spn-196489","text":". And "},{"id":"spn-196490","marks":["code"],"text":"test/weave-hvm4-run.mjs"},{"id":"spn-196491","text":" wires the real HVM4 backend (6/6 differential agreement), confirming the certificate is substrate-independent."}]},{"id":"blk-119378","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-196492","text":"What remains genuinely open: the polynomial "},{"id":"spn-196493","marks":["bold"],"text":"degree"},{"id":"spn-196494","text":" is still "},{"id":"spn-196495","marks":["italic"],"text":"measured"},{"id":"spn-196496","text":", not statically inferred. Pinning it by type is "},{"id":"spn-196497","marks":["bold"],"text":"static LAL"},{"id":"spn-196498","text":" inference (Light Affine Logic / Baillot–Terui §-boxes) — the named boundary. EAL gives the certified "},{"id":"spn-196499","marks":["italic"],"text":"tower height"},{"id":"spn-196500","text":"; LAL would give the certified "},{"id":"spn-196501","marks":["italic"],"text":"degree"},{"id":"spn-196502","text":"."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraw4vlculcvfyu6qsxvuho3re46iro2p3bn6x5y3pohuz4enmp5eja","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}